From 1bd3a5b6633ea8e79bf52e58787c06e8ee31b519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huangserva <huangserva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:14:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] feat(sm70/tp2): Qwen3.8-27B two-GPU tensor parallel
 (NCCL in graph)

Two processes, one per V100, each loading a rank artifact from
tools/tp2/shard_qwen38_27b.py. Row-parallel projections all-reduce the
residual in place; column-parallel projections run on half shapes gated
by NINFER_VOLTA_BUILD.

Fixes found in bring-up:
- rank 1 MLP down now zeroes its destination and reuses linear_add:
  linear's wide-T MMA route misreads QPN-prepacked NVFP4 weights
  (prefill residual cosine vs single card was 0.38, now 0.9996).
- 12/2 attention uses the 24/4 verify routing so MTP verify never falls
  to the prompt kernel (was 150 ms per call at 186K).

186K code 52.0 -> 70.1 tok/s, 193K zh 40.0 -> 56.9, 186K TTFT 379 -> 249 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
